#heading(level: 2, numbering: none)[Notes on the literature]
<notes:residual-currents>

#notes-on(
  <sec:main-facts>,
  <sec:normal-intersections>,
  <sec:main-theorem>,
) Some special cases of local definitions of the residue and the principal value
on a manifold were introduced by Dolbeault @bib:Dolbeault1956, Norguet
@bib:Norguet1959a, and Schwartz @bib:Schwartz1953. Later Dolbeault
@bib:Dolbeault1970a, @bib:Dolbeault1971a, @bib:Dolbeault1971b constructed
canonical currents that extend meromorphic forms on manifolds and coincide with
the principal value. On analytic spaces final results for residual currents and
principal values in codimension 1 were obtained by Herrera and Lieberman
@bib:Herrera1971.

The existence of a residual current $R_f$ and a principal value $R_(f') P_(f_p)$
in codimension $p > 1$ was proved by Coleff and Herrera @bib:Coleff1978. They
gave a representation of the principal value by a repeated limit
(@ss:iterated-limit), and also a description of supports (@ss:supports-general).
Preliminary results were obtained by Herrera @bib:Herrera1973, @bib:Herrera1974.
The currents $R_I P_J$ were considered by Passare @bib:Pettersson1984;
correspondingly he proved the first part of the main theorem of @sec:main-facts.

#notes-on(<sec:residual-currents>, <sec:fibered-residues>) The result of
@ss:nonpolar-principal-value was obtained by Coleff and Herrera @bib:Coleff1978.
Leray's residue formula for polar sets with singularities is a sharpening of the
formula (ii) in @ss:fibered-local-residues (due to Coleff and Herrera) and
apparently they noted it for the first time. The nondegeneracy of a residual
current (@ss:nondegeneracy) was noted by Passare @bib:Pettersson1984. The
algebraic aspect of this nondegeneracy was considered by Ramis and Ruget
@bib:Ramis1974. The results of @sec:fibered-residues are due to Coleff and
Herrera @bib:Coleff1978.
